                    'content' => '<p>Unlike WordPress, Laravel, or Drupal, there is no community marketplace for pre-built plugins, themes, or widgets. If a project requires a complex feature (such as forums, advanced SEO analyzers, or newsletters), the developer must implement the models, controllers, and views from scratch inside self-contained modules.</p>',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'text',
                    'title' => '3. Single Database Tenancy Scaling Limits',
                    'content' => '<p>Zero CMS isolates multiple discrete site tenants inside a unified single database using time-ordered UUIDv7 and schema scoping (<code>site_id</code>). While this eliminates multiple database connection overheads and allows unified server maintenance, it means all tenants share the same database server resource pool. Under extreme high-throughput loads, resource contention (CPU, disk I/O, or connection limits) can degrade performance across all tenants.</p>',
