                    'content' => '<p>The custom TCP socket mailer wraps the payload inside strict, multi-boundary MIME headers to support clean HTML templates, attachments, and UTF-8 encoding natively offline.</p>',
                ],
            ],
            'type' => 'page',
            'show_in_nav' => '0',
        ],
        [
            'title' => 'Multi-Tenant Data Isolation',
            'slug' => 'docs/how-tos/multitenancy',
            'status' => 'published',
            'site_domain' => 'd6laptop.zero.guide',
            'content' => [
                [
                    'type' => 'text',
                    'title' => 'Multi-Tenant Architecture Overview',
                    'content' => '<p>In multi-tenant SaaS structures, multiple discrete sites (tenants) share a single database, codebase, and web server container. To guarantee absolute security, **no tenant must ever be allowed to see, query, or leak data belonging to another tenant!**</p>',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'text',
                    'title' => 'Physical Schema Scoping (site_id)',
                    'content' => '<p>To enforce this boundary at the database level, **every single database table** in Zero CMS (including order items, variants, pages, and posts) physically possesses a <code>site_id</code> column string index.</p>',
