        [
            'title' => 'Creating Custom Page Builder Blocks',
            'slug' => 'docs/how-tos/custom-blocks',
            'status' => 'published',
            'site_domain' => 'd6laptop.zero.guide',
            'content' => [
                [
                    'type' => 'text',
                    'title' => 'Introduction to Block-Based Architectures',
                    'content' => '<p>Zero CMS features an extremely powerful, high-contrast, zero-dependency Page Builder Block System. Pages are stored in the database as serialized JSON blocks (under the <code>content</code> field). To build an active, beautiful block inside the CMS, you need to configure its <strong>Frontend View Template</strong> (to render the block beautifully on the public website) and register it in the <strong>Core Block Registry</strong> (which automatically generates admin edit fields, handles inserting drawers, and serializes inputs generically!).</p>',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'text',
                    'title' => 'Step 1: Create the Frontend View Template',
                    'content' => '<p>Frontend blocks are resolved dynamically by the theme template renderer. To add a block template named <code>accordion</code>, create a new PHP file at <code>src/Views/themes/default/blocks/accordion.php</code>. This template receives a local <code>$block</code> array data context populated with fields:</p><pre><code class="language-php">&lt;?php
// src/Views/themes/default/blocks/accordion.php
$items = $block[\'items\'] ?? [];
?&gt;
&lt;div class="block-accordion"&gt;
  &lt;?php if (!empty($block[\'title\'])): ?&gt;
    &lt;h3&gt;&lt;?php echo htmlspecialchars($block[\'title\']); ?&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
  &lt;?php endif; ?&gt;
  
  &lt;div class="accordion-list"&gt;
    &lt;?php foreach ($items as $item): ?&gt;
      &lt;div class="accordion-item"&gt;
        &lt;div class="accordion-trigger"&gt;&lt;?php echo htmlspecialchars($item[\'title\'] ?? \'\'); ?&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div class="accordion-panel"&gt;&lt;?php echo htmlspecialchars($item[\'content\'] ?? \'\'); ?&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;?php endforeach; ?&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'text',
                    'title' => 'Step 2: Create the Admin Edit Fields View Template',
                    'content' => '<p>Create a self-contained PHP file representing the administrative edit fields for the block at <code>src/Modules/Admin/Views/blocks/accordion.php</code>. This template is automatically included and pre-rendered inside the admin page builder blocks list. Use convention-based input classes to enable automatic serialization:</p><pre><code class="language-html">&lt;div class="field-group"&gt;
    &lt;label&gt;Block Title&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;input type="text" class="block-title-input" value="&lt;?php echo htmlspecialchars($blockTitle); ?&gt;"&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="field-group"&gt;
    &lt;label&gt;Accordion Items&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;div class="accordion-items-list"&gt;
        &lt;!-- Dynamic items rows --&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;button type="button" class="btn-add-accordion-item"&gt;+ Add Accordion Item&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'text',
                    'title' => 'Step 3: Register the Block in the Core App',
                    'content' => '<p>Register your block dynamically inside the core <code>App::bootstrap()</code> method (or inside any bootstrapper/module initialization) by calling <code>App::registerBlock()</code>:</p><pre><code class="language-php">// Inside src/Core/App.php

self::registerBlock(\'accordion\', [
    \'label\' => \'Accordion FAQ List\',
    \'description\' => \'A sleek list of expandable/collapsible questions and answers.\',
    \'icon\' => \'file\'
]);</code></pre><p>This single registration completely takes care of generating card options in the Block Inserter modal drawer, injecting templates inside the builder container, and serializing complex input arrays into the database payload dynamically on the fly!</p>',
                ],
            ],
            'type' => 'page',
            'show_in_nav' => '0',
