            'title' => 'Setting Up Supervisor for the Job Queue',
            'slug' => 'docs/how-tos/supervisor-setup',
            'status' => 'published',
            'show_in_nav' => '0',
            'site_domain' => 'd6laptop.zero.guide',
            'content' => [
                [
                    'type' => 'text',
                    'title' => 'Introduction',
                    'content' => '<p>To ensure background queue tasks are processed continuously in production, it is highly recommended to run the Zero CMS Job Queue Runner as a monitored background daemon using **Supervisor**. Supervisor acts as a process manager that launches our executable binary on boot and automatically restarts it if it crashes, runs out of memory, or encounters system bottlenecks.</p>',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'text',
                    'title' => 'Supervisor Configuration',
                    'content' => '<p>Create a new Supervisor configuration file under <code>/etc/supervisor/conf.d/zero-queue.conf</code>:</p><pre><code class="language-ini">[program:zero-queue-worker]
process_name=%(program_name)s_%(process_num)02d
directory=/data/misc/zero/
command=php bin/queue-runner
autostart=true
autorestart=true
user=www-data
numprocs=1
redirect_stderr=true
stdout_logfile=/data/misc/zero/storage/logs/queue-worker.log</code></pre>',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'text',
                    'title' => 'Activating the Daemon',
                    'content' => '<p>To register, load, and launch your newly configured process manager, execute the following commands in your server terminal:</p><pre><code class="language-bash"># Reread and discover new configuration files
sudo supervisorctl reread

# Add and start the newly discovered background worker
sudo supervisorctl update

# Verify the status and verify that the daemon is active and running
sudo supervisorctl status</code></pre>',
                ],
                [
                    'type' => 'text',
                    'title' => 'Monitoring and Log Rotation',
                    'content' => '<p>All standard outputs, processing durations, and exceptions are logged directly to <code>/data/misc/zero/storage/logs/queue-worker.log</code>. To prevent this file from expanding infinitely over time, configure standard log rotation under <code>/etc/logrotate.d/zero-queue</code>:</p><pre><code class="language-text">/data/misc/zero/storage/logs/queue-worker.log {
    weekly
    missingok
    rotate 12
    compress
    notifempty
    sharedscripts
}</code></pre>',
                ],
            ],
            'type' => 'page',
