        [
            'title' => 'Security & Threat Auditing Module',
            'slug' => 'docs/modules/security',
            'status' => 'published',
            'show_in_nav' => '0',
            'site_domain' => 'd6laptop.zero.guide',
            'content' => [
                [
                    'type' => 'text',
                    'title' => 'Decoupled Platform Security & Telemetry',
                    'content' => '<p>The Zero CMS Security Module provides unified back-office auditing, security telemetry, dynamic exploit risk scoring, and automated compliance auditing. It strictly separates from the Core CMS Kernel, allowing administrators to monitor system integrity and logs cleanly from a dedicated security panel.</p><h4>Core Capabilities</h4><ul><li><strong>Dynamic Telemetry Scoring:</strong> Evaluates live system parameters (such as default passwords, install files, writable folders, and admins headcount) to compile an active integrity score out of 100.</li><li><strong>Database Security Audits:</strong> Persists security scans, warnings, and audit logs into dedicated <code>security_audits</code> and <code>audit_logs</code> MySQL tables recursively.</li><li><strong>Automated Audit Log Purging:</strong> Leverages background jobs to clean up outdated transaction logs, maintaining database efficiency and multi-tenant isolation.</li></ul>',
